# Paths chezmoi should DELETE from $HOME on every apply.
#
# Removing a file from the source directory does not remove it from $HOME —
# chezmoi simply stops managing it. This file is how a path is actually retired
# across all three hosts.

# Hand-copied nvim-lspconfig server configs. Replaced by the nvim-lspconfig
# plugin plus vim.lsp.config() overrides in lua/core/lsp.lua; left in place they
# would still be merged onto the runtimepath and shadow the plugin's versions
# with a stale copy.
.config/nvim/lsp

# Old hand-written fontconfig: CJK embolden rules for fonts none of these hosts
# have (Song/Sun/Kai/Ming) plus a <dir>~/.fonts</dir> that no longer exists. It
# was dropped from the source directory in 4a97d61 but stayed behind in $HOME on
# every host. Font policy now lives in .config/fontconfig/conf.d/ instead, and
# leaving this file in place would keep it loaded alongside.
.config/fontconfig/fonts.conf

# Dead cava launcher. It piped the standalone `cava` binary through sed into a
# custom/ module, but that binary is not installed on any host and no waybar
# module ever referenced the script: the bar uses waybar-cava's built-in `cava`
# module, which links libcava in-process. Left in $HOME it is an executable that
# looks load-bearing and is not.
.config/waybar/scripts/cava.sh
